## Rules for every task agent

- Edit only the files your brief names, and in them only what it names. Never
  edit a test, anything under `agents/`, or anything in this directory except
  `progress.md`.
- Do not open files your brief does not name. The signatures in your brief are
  all you may depend on. If they are not enough, your task is under-specified:
  stop and reply `blocked: <what is missing>`. Do not guess.
- Do not change a signature or doc comment, add a dependency, or improve
  neighbouring code.
- Run your brief's verify commands before you reply. The orchestrator runs
  them again; report exactly what passed and what did not.
- Commits: __COMMIT_POLICY__

## Progress log

Read `progress.md` before you start. Lines beginning `HUMAN NOTE:` are steering
from the user and override anything else there. When you finish, done or
blocked, append:

```
## <ISO timestamp> · <task id> · <title>
- Changed: <files>
- Verified: <each command and its result>
- Learnings: <specific, technical gotchas the next agent should know; or "none">
---
```
